## Architecture summary (so next agent picking this up has context)

1. **`<pi-entity-list>` is a drop-in shell** — handles server-side pagination, 300ms-debounced search, loading skeleton, empty state, error toast. Page supplies `[columns]`, `[rowActions]`, `(create)`, optional `(rowClick)`.
2. **Page owns column definitions** (not DSL) so column logic stays with business layer.
3. **Page owns dialog lifecycle** — creates PiRowActionsComponent template, opens EntityFormDialogComponent, refreshOnDialogClose stub (TODO once entity-list exposes `reload()`, currently surfaces a toast on delete only).
4. **Backend sortBy discipline** — only `/api/products` accepts `sortBy`. Marking `sortable: true` on pages without backend support causes 400.
5. **All migrated pages now use AlertDialogComponent for delete** with predictable Russian copy + `extractErrorMessage(res.error)` for failure.

## Out-of-scope notes

- `inventory/storage-items.page.ts` and `inventory/stock-movements.page.ts` were already migrated in Wave 3 (TZ-232.C). Combined with this Wave 2, total pages on `<pi-entity-list>` shell: **7**.
